Description: keep host tools from linking the target libraries
 The gyp "host" toolset targets (node_js2c here, plus the ones covered by the
 v8.gyp and icu-generic.gyp patches) inherit the global `libraries` list that
 common.gypi builds up for --shared-openssl/--shared-zlib/--shared-cares and
 friends.  In a cross build those resolve against the target staging tree, so
 the host binary would try to link foreign objects.  `libraries!` replaces the
 inherited list for these targets only.
 Node 24 moved the simdutf dependency of node_js2c into a `conditions` block,
 so the Node 20 anchor no longer matches; the insertion is re-anchored on the
 target header instead.
--- a/node.gyp
+++ b/node.gyp
@@ -1612,6 +1612,7 @@
       'target_name': 'node_js2c',
       'type': 'executable',
       'toolsets': ['host'],
+      'libraries!':[ '-licui18n', '-licuuc', '-licudata', '-lcrypto', '-lssl', '-lz', '-lhttp_parser', '-luv', '-lnghttp2', '-lcares' ],
       'include_dirs': [
         'tools',
         'src',
